cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article that
  introduces the protocol.
title: "treatment-identity: verify that the treatment an experiment declares is the one its data loader delivers"
abstract: >-
  Six CPU gates and a per-run certificate that assert what a training pipeline
  delivers to the optimiser, rather than what its configuration requests. The
  gates run against synthetic fixtures in seconds, before any GPU budget is
  committed, and fail on unexpected equality as well as unexpected difference.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/uselessai/treatment-identity"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - data loaders
  - metamorphic testing
  - experiment validity
  - synthetic degradation
